<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Yamani</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. 712 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century-bce">8th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Yamani was a usurper who seized the throne of the Philistine city of Ashdod around 712 BCE after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assyrian-empire">Assyrians</a> had deposed its king. He led a revolt against Assyria in hope of Egyptian support, but when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sargon-ii">Sargon II</a>'s army arrived he fled to Kush, whose king later handed him over to the Assyrians. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sargon-of-akkad">Sargon</a> then reorganised Ashdod as an Assyrian province.</p></div>
